      "title": "Kinodynamic Pose Optimization for Humanoid Loco-Manipulation",
      "takeaway": "This method paper addresses humanoid robots pushing heavy objects by combining kinodynamic pose optimization with loco-manipulation model predictive control (MPC). The pose optimization plans the optimal pushing pose using an object-robot dynamics model, robot kinematic constraints, and object parameters, while the MPC tracks this pose by coordinating pushing and ground reaction forces for stable locomotion. Numerical validation shows the pose optimization solves as a nonlinear programming (NLP) problem in an average of 250 ms, enabling the robot to push objects up to 20 kg (118% of its mass) and recover from a 120 N force disturbance. Inspect how the pose optimization integrates the dynamics model and constraints, and how the MPC coordinates forces to maintain stability during heavy pushing.",
